.TH WB\-UPGRADE 1 "" "watchbill"
.SH NAME
wb\-upgrade \- pin the repository to the installed revision
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBwb\fR upgrade [\-\-dry\-run | \-n] [\-q | \-\-quiet]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Pin the repository to the installed revision: copy its files over .watchbill/revision/, removing those it does not have, and its manifest to .watchbill/revision.sha256, set the lines watchbill: and revision: of watchbill.yml, and add each pattern the installed wb init would write that the file lacks; no other line is changed. It says each write first, then writes, runs the check of wb check and says the command that commits the change: it commits nothing. \-\-dry\-run (\-n) says the same and writes nothing.
.PP
Ends with 0 when it is done and the check holds, or there is nothing to do; 1 when it is refused (a change under .watchbill/ that is not committed, an installed version older than the pinned one) or the check does not hold; 2 when it was used wrongly or the repository is not set up.
.PP
\-q (\-\-quiet) leaves out the lines that confirm the writes and the line that says there is nothing to do, and not what it says before it writes, a refusal, a difference of the check, or that nothing is committed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run, \-n
Say the same and write nothing.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Leave out the lines that only confirm what was done or say there was nothing to do; never a refusal, a warning, what is said before a write, or a command the person has to run.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
It is done and the check holds, or there is nothing to do.
.TP
.B 1
It is refused (a change under .watchbill/ that is not committed, an installed version older than the pinned one) or the check does not hold.
.TP
.B 2
It was used wrongly or the repository is not set up.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wb (1) ,
.BR wb\-check (1) ,
.BR wb\-init (1)
